hexagon: version 2 of the chunked gated delta net kernel

The cost

On the phone (HTP0, Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0, one prefill ubatch of 1024 tokens) the
chunked kernel of GATED_DELTA_NET takes 128 ms of the 1044 ms of the
ubatch, 5.3 to 5.65 ms for each of the 24 layers. The PMU stage of
2026-09-24 shows an op that the HVX instruction count bounds (1.82
instructions per packet), with the HMX busy 9 % of the op and each HMX job
between two HVX phases. The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target gdnk, the v79
timing model) gives the split of the HVX work: the forward substitution
takes 4 packets for each multiply-add (a conversion to IEEE after each
product and each sum), the two transposes of K use vector scatters (about
45 cycles each), the gates of a head come from scalar reads of VTCM (about
27 cycles each), and a 32 x 32 transpose keeps 64 vectors on the stack.

The change

kernel_params[1] = 2 selects version 2 in gdn-chunk-ops.c. Version 1 stays
unchanged for the A/B runs. Version 2 keeps the dataflow and changes these
things:
- The products take the plain tiles of K, Q and V. The per-token factors go
  to the small operands: W = T' K with T' = T diag(beta e^gamma), U = T'' V
  with T'' = T diag(beta), S_upd = K^T Delta' with Delta' = diag(e^(gamma_C
  - gamma)) Delta. Thus K, Q and V each convert to f16 tiles once.
- One transpose of K gives the weight of A and P and the input of S_upd.
  It is a 32-bit shuffle transpose of the f16 rows through 4 KB of VTCM.
- The forward substitution does two rows together, keeps qfloat sums,
  skips the half of a row of T that is zero, and sets the lanes above the
  diagonal to +0.
- Each operand of an HVX multiply is 2^-50 or more, or +0: the smaller
  values flush to +0. A strong decay makes values near the end of the f32
  range. In the kernel lab a qfloat sum of such products gave -1.6e38 and
  -inf where the true value is about 1e-39 (target gdnsolve).
- A chunk with a zero coefficient in the forward substitution (a strong
  decay flushes E to +0) takes the solve with the arithmetic of version 1:
  each product and each sum goes to f32 at once, and a term with a zero
  coefficient does not run. On the phone (stage gdnk2, gates from -20) the
  qfloat sums of the paired solve gave values near 2^105 for such chunks,
  with A' and beta finite and at most 1, where the lab gives values below
  10. Version 1 gives correct results for the same chunks. The chunk decay
  of the state update takes no multiply when it is zero.
- The HMX product takes any tile strides, thus one tile set serves as an
  activation and as a weight.
- The DMA brings the gate and beta of the head as one column each.
- Each HMX job runs beside the HVX work that it does not touch: m1 beside
  the state update of the chunk before, m2 beside the output store of the
  chunk before, m3 beside the loads and tiles of the next chunk. The output
  rows go to DDR by DMA.
- The op can apply the L2 norm of q and k when it loads them (gdn-step.h,
  kernel_params[2..6]). The sequential kernel, the fused state step and the
  tail tokens of the chunked kernel take the same norm. The host does not
  ask for it in this patch.

GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CHUNK=2 is the new preset value. 1 selects version 1, and
0 the sequential kernel for each batch.

The results

The kernel lab, timing model, 12 heads of 128, 512 tokens, 6 threads. The
model does not time the HMX, and the lab does each DMA transfer as a
memcpy on the thread. Thus the comparison uses the cycles of the kernel
functions on the threads:
    version 1    6.62 M cycles, 69.0 k for each row and chunk of 64 tokens
    version 2    4.46 M cycles, 46.4 k for each row and chunk of 64 tokens
The cycles of version 2 are 67 % of those of version 1. The forward
substitution goes from 3.36 M cycles (phase b of version 1) to 1.78 M
(phase solve of version 2, which also makes A', P', T' and T''). The
flushes to +0 and the f32 solve of the chunks with a zero coefficient
cost 0.94 M of the 4.46 M cycles. Without them, version 2 took 3.52 M
cycles, but the phone gave values that are not finite.

The functional runs against a float64 reference of the recurrence, with
the HMX in the functional mode (the bound of test-backend-ops is 2e-6):
    tokens  K  heads  gate from  norm  NMSE attention  NMSE state
    128     1  4      -0.5       no    3.37e-07        2.36e-07
    128     1  4      -8         no    3.25e-07        2.08e-07
    128     1  4      -20        no    3.28e-07        1.94e-07
    512     1  2      -0.5       no    3.56e-07        2.19e-07
    70      1  4      -0.5       no    3.14e-07        3.03e-07
    70      1  4 x 64 -3         yes   2.59e-07        1.96e-07
    100     3  4      -0.5       yes   3.17e-07        6.34e-08
    165     5  4      -0.5       yes   3.36e-07        3.27e-08
    512     1  2      -0.5       yes   3.56e-07        2.19e-07
The heads have 128 values, and 4 x 64 is 4 heads of 64 values. The
snapshot slots of the K = 3 and K = 5 runs give 1.16e-07 and 8.71e-08.
Version 1 gives 3.11e-07 and 1.46e-07 for 128 tokens from -8. Each HMX job
gives the same bits when it runs before or after the HVX phase beside it
(--defer 1, 128 tokens, and 165 tokens with the norm). Thus no phase
writes an input of that job or reads its output.

The phone stage gdnk of 2026-09-25 (HTP0, Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0) runs one build
of the series with four switch settings. Variant C adds this patch to
variant B (the conv DMA), and variant A is the kernels before the series.
In one prefill ubatch of 1024 tokens, GATED_DELTA_NET takes 93.0 ms of DSP
op time in place of 129.3 ms (the median of 6 graphs). test-backend-ops
perf, the median of 2 rounds:
    case                                    B          C
    16 k heads, 32 v heads, 1024 tokens     5191 us    3112 us
    32 heads, 1024 tokens, gates from -20   5911 us    4108 us
pp512 gives 1061.5 t/s for C and 1014.6 t/s for A, and tg32 gives 10.67
and 10.69 t/s. The stage gdnk2 of 2026-09-25 gives the KL divergence of
the prefill path against the naive x86 base: 0.000588 +- 0.000042 for C
and 0.000584 +- 0.000040 for A. The op tests of C and of the whole series
pass.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

